      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "fact_5",
      "value": "Three gods, Brahma, Vishnu, and Shiva, and other deities are considered manifestations of and are worshipped as incarnations of Brahman.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0047",
        "chunk_title": "Notes",
        "chunk_order": 46,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "fact_6",
      "value": "The members of various Hindu sects worship many specific deities and follow innumerable rites in honor of specific gods, which are seen as expressions of the same unchanging reality.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
        "chunk_id": "page_0047",
        "chunk_title": "Notes",
        "chunk_order": 46,
        "source_type": "page"
      }
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "field": "fact_7",
      "value": "While Hindus believe in many devas, many are monotheistic and recognize only one Supreme Being, a God or Goddess who is the source and ruler of the devas.",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
